title: Firedamp
subtitle: An explosion underground.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('mine_disaster'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('mine_disaster');
if (!Q.lw_pit) { Q.lw_pit = 'a pit at ' + Q.lw_town; }
Q.lw_dead = RG.lw.rnd(18, 84);
Q.lw_pit_town = Q.lw_pit.replace(/^.* at /, '').replace(/^.* near /, '');
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {militancy: 6});
RG.news(Q.lw_dead + ' miners killed in explosion at ' + Q.lw_pit_town, 3);
RG.ledger(Q.lw_dead + ' miners died in an explosion at ' + Q.lw_pit + '.', 'lw_mine_' + (Q.lw_fired.mine_disaster || 1));
!}

= Firedamp

At the change of shift, an explosion of firedamp tore through the deepest seam of **[+ lw_pit +]**, in [+ lw_d_name +]. The rescue teams worked for three days. They brought up [+ lw_dead +] bodies, and a pit pony that had somehow lived.

The company says it was an act of God. The miners say the ventilation was cut back in the spring to save money, and that the safety man who complained was moved to the surface. Everyone in the pit village knows somebody on the list.

The funerals are on Saturday. The whole district will be there, and it will be looking at who speaks.

- @strike: Call the coalfield out in a political strike.
- @socialise: Make it the case for taking the mines from the owners.
- @relief: Bury the dead and feed the families.
- @inquiry: Demand a safety inquiry with the miners' union.

@strike
subtitle: The district stops for its dead. Militancy rises, and the police come with it. The Left's answer.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
RG.startStrike(Q.lw_d);
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {militancy: 5, repression: 5, members: 0.03});
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 2, 6);
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 0, -3);
!}

From the graveside, our speaker calls for every pit to stop until the owners answer for the dead. The next morning, the winding gear is still across the district.

@socialise
subtitle: The old demand of the revolution, with the dead as evidence. Worker support grows. The Spartacist line.
on-arrival: {!
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.stability -= 1;
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {loyalty: 4});
RG.news('Communists: the mines to the people after ' + Q.lw_pit_town);
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 2, 5);
!}

The coal owners promised in 1919 that the mines would be socialised, and set up a commission. The commission is still sitting. Our leaflet prints its members' names next to the names of the dead.

@relief
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The party is there when it matters. The district will remember.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {loyalty: 9, members: 0.05});
Q.worker_support += 1;
Q.unity += 1;
!}

The party pays for the coffins nobody else would pay for, and our women's group runs the kitchen in the pit village for a month. At the funeral, the red flag is on every third coffin.

@inquiry
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Through the union, a real inquiry and new safety rules. The Right's way.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids working through the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('union_work');
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.spd_relation += 2;
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {militancy: -3, loyalty: 3});
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 2, 5);
!}

Our comrades in the miners' union force a joint inquiry. It finds that the ventilation was cut back. The manager is fined, and the pits of the district get safety men elected by the miners.
